# Vanilla NPC name replacements here
# for later use
NPCName: {
}

Bestiary_FlavorText: {
	# Bosses
	npc_HallowBoss: The most gluttonous prismatic fairy to ever inhabit Terraria, rumored to have eaten a titaness whole and alive, body and soul, to gain her modern-day size and strength. She wishes to one day shine with the feast-worthy, fattening light of the digested sun.
	# Caverns
	npc_Nymph: Masterfully deceives the common fool by posing as a lost adventurer looking to trade, then lunges forward and gobbles up their prey before they can so much as touch them. Also enjoys certain card and board games.
	# Forest
	npc_Butterfly: Beautiful fluttering insects that love sunrises and tasty flowers. Fish are attracted to these based on their color variety and how healthily they've been eating.
	# Hallow
	npc_EmpressButterfly: The collective foremothers and forefathers of all prismatic fairies, these beautiful little butterflies are one of the favorite foods of many fairies, including the hallowed 'goddess' herself.
	# Rain
	npc_FlyingFish: A peculiar species of fish which gains the ability to swim through the sky when it rains. While they aren't averse to gobbling up those that bother them, be they seafood, land-dwellers, or aviators, they're actually quite docile otherwise.
	# Solar Eclipse
	npc_ThePossessed: Oftentimes, under the Eclipse's blacklight glow, malevolent spirits will set out to possess once-meek peasants like this unfortunate girl and glut themselves on the unprepared.
	# Town NPCs
	npc_Nurse: A freelance nurseenary, if you can call that a word, that earned her medical license basically entirely to have an excuse to try to pack some bums onto her bum. Much to her chagrin, everyone seems to stick around top-side for her...
	npc_Dryad: While dryads are rarely found in civilized country, they are more plentiful than you'd think; this one in particular is very hung up on the idea that the world is impure. Given how often her people and ancestors alike get churned by vegans and vegetarians, this isn't a surprise.
	npc_Stylist: Originally hailing from northwest Avarsici, Amber eventually found herself running away when her best gal pal was outcast from their hometown. She's still a stellar hair styler, though, and she and her gut will gladly whip your hair up nice!
	npc_Mechanic: A masterful robotics worker whose exact country of origin is unknown; only that she was held against her will by a mysterious group to make new parts for an equally mysterious master.
}
